1
00:00:01,802 --> 00:00:05,438
(The darkness slowly fades away.)

2
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:08,807
(Morning arrives in Chiang Mai.)

3
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:12,178
(Lush with fresh greenery)

4
00:00:12,779 --> 00:00:15,748
(Elephants roam peacefully
in this serene setting.)

5
00:00:16,617 --> 00:00:22,055
(Elephant Hotel)

6
00:00:22,923 --> 00:00:27,994
(They're still fast asleep in their room,
exhausted from the elephant date.)

7
00:00:30,564 --> 00:00:33,499
(Outside the room)

8
00:00:39,006 --> 00:00:44,644
(An elephant wanders outside their room.)

9
00:00:51,378 --> 00:00:52,211
What's that sound?

10
00:00:55,188 --> 00:00:56,688
What?

11
00:00:56,689 --> 00:00:57,556
What is it?

12
00:00:58,392 --> 00:00:59,325
An elephant!

13
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:01,293
There's an elephant out there!

14
00:01:01,294 --> 00:01:02,661
It's an elephant!

15
00:01:03,464 --> 00:01:06,332
(Ta-da!)

16
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:08,368
- So cute!
- She's right in front of us.

17
00:01:08,369 --> 00:01:10,403
They really do visit.

18
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:11,670
What is she doing?

19
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:13,873
- So cute!
- She's saying hello!

20
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:15,274
Cute!

21
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:16,108
Let's go outside.

22
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:17,276
(Stepping out to meet the elephant)

23
00:01:18,045 --> 00:01:19,545
- Wow.
- Is she saying hi?

24
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:20,604
(Filmed safely under expert supervision)

25
00:01:20,881 --> 00:01:22,081
Hello!

26
00:01:22,683 --> 00:01:24,117
- Cute!
- Adorable!

27
00:01:24,118 --> 00:01:25,351
(The elephant waves her trunk.)

28
00:01:25,352 --> 00:01:28,121
She's so sweet. Hello!

29
00:01:28,856 --> 00:01:30,190
Can we feed her?

30
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:31,624
We can feed her!

31
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:34,860
- She's so cute!
- Adorable.

32
00:01:34,861 --> 00:01:36,261
(A bag of elephant treats
awaits outside the door.)

33
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:40,065
(Handing over the bag)

34
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:41,434
She's adorable.

35
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:42,201
(Waiting patiently)

36
00:01:42,202 --> 00:01:43,402
Here you go!

37
00:01:43,804 --> 00:01:44,837
Let me give you some.

38
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:46,139
(Munching away)

39
00:01:46,373 --> 00:01:47,506
Here, have some.

40
00:01:47,507 --> 00:01:48,641
You must be hungry.

41
00:01:49,543 --> 00:01:51,210
You're hungry, aren't you?

42
00:01:52,046 --> 00:01:54,213
You're such a pretty girl.

43
00:01:54,548 --> 00:01:56,949
- She's pretty.
- Yeah, she really is.

44
00:01:57,384 --> 00:02:00,119
You're so pretty!

45
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,188
You're holding still.
You understood me, didn't you?

46
00:02:04,425 --> 00:02:06,859
She's so cute.
She looks nice and clean today.

47
00:02:07,928 --> 00:02:09,095
Here you go.

48
00:02:09,096 --> 00:02:10,196
You're hungry.

49
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,197
- She's so cute.
- Here, eat up.

50
00:02:12,198 --> 00:02:13,766
(Sian gathers up his courage.)

51
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,101
She's so cute! What should I do?

52
00:02:18,672 --> 00:02:19,639
Crunchy!

53
00:02:21,909 --> 00:02:22,976
You're scared again.

54
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:24,277
You're scared, aren't you?

55
00:02:24,511 --> 00:02:25,811
(Embarrassed)

56
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,213
- I'm...
- You chickened out again.

57
00:02:27,214 --> 00:02:28,514
I'm still a bit nervous.

58
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:31,884
(Reaching out carefully)

59
00:02:32,452 --> 00:02:34,019
(Gently)

60
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,421
(Shaking)

61
00:02:35,689 --> 00:02:36,956
I saw that!

62
00:02:36,957 --> 00:02:37,990
(Forever timid)

63
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:39,992
She's so sweet.

64
00:02:41,128 --> 00:02:43,429
I'm used to her now.

65
00:02:44,899 --> 00:02:46,432
She looks like Dumbo.

66
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:47,867
- Doesn't she?
- Yeah!

67
00:02:48,468 --> 00:02:50,135
You have such pretty eyes.

68
00:02:51,204 --> 00:02:52,672
Her feet are adorable too.

69
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,307
They're so cute!

70
00:02:54,308 --> 00:02:58,344
(Pretty from every single angle)

71
00:02:58,879 --> 00:03:00,947
She's gorgeous. This is incredible.

72
00:03:03,029 --> 00:03:04,930
An elephant wake-up call.

73
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:07,152
I'm wide awake now.

74
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:09,488
I'm not sleepy at all anymore.

75
00:03:09,590 --> 00:03:12,058
Wait, she's not the one
we walked with yesterday.

76
00:03:12,059 --> 00:03:13,927
Isn't she the one we bathed with?

77
00:03:13,928 --> 00:03:15,328
No, she's a different elephant.

78
00:03:15,329 --> 00:03:17,730
(Soaking up all the attention)

79
00:03:20,767 --> 00:03:22,768
(The elephant suddenly walks away.)

80
00:03:24,271 --> 00:03:25,838
(Trying to figure out what just happened)

81
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:28,274
Wait, she wasn't our elephant?

82
00:03:28,575 --> 00:03:30,010
She wasn't meant for our room?

83
00:03:30,444 --> 00:03:32,378
She wasn't assigned to us?

84
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:34,480
She just saw the food and went wild.

85
00:03:34,481 --> 00:03:35,715
- Was she just making a detour?
- What?

86
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,682
Really?

87
00:03:36,817 --> 00:03:38,351
She was on her way to a different room.

88
00:03:39,019 --> 00:03:40,487
That's why she looked unfamiliar.

89
00:03:42,623 --> 00:03:44,424
- She's the grandma!
- Grandma!

90
00:03:44,858 --> 00:03:46,025
Hello!

91
00:03:46,159 --> 00:03:48,293
- She brought her mom along!
- Hi!

92
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,596
Good morning, Grandma!

93
00:03:50,931 --> 00:03:52,565
Here, have some food.

94
00:03:52,566 --> 00:03:53,699
(Feeding the elephants right away)

95
00:03:55,802 --> 00:03:57,236
There you go.

96
00:03:57,538 --> 00:03:58,604
Okay.

97
00:04:00,273 --> 00:04:01,340
(Patting)

98
00:04:01,341 --> 00:04:02,274
Wait.

99
00:04:03,276 --> 00:04:04,876
- Easy there.
- They're getting eager.

100
00:04:05,512 --> 00:04:06,545
Step back a little.

101
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:09,882
- Back up.
- Back up, back up.

102
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:11,617
Hold this.

103
00:04:13,553 --> 00:04:17,356
She drooled all over my foot!

104
00:04:18,659 --> 00:04:19,959
Again?

105
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:21,260
Here she goes again.

106
00:04:21,261 --> 00:04:23,229
(Shoving her trunk right into the bag)

107
00:04:23,230 --> 00:04:25,464
- Hey, no!
- She grabbed a huge handful.

108
00:04:26,032 --> 00:04:27,633
(Snarfing it down)

109
00:04:27,634 --> 00:04:29,120
What does it taste like?

110
00:04:29,236 --> 00:04:30,570
It smells really sweet.

111
00:04:31,019 --> 00:04:31,971
Give it a tiny taste.

112
00:04:32,306 --> 00:04:33,373
She wants that one.

113
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:36,608
They eat 250 kg a day.

114
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:39,011
Just one bag weighs 30 kg.

115
00:04:39,813 --> 00:04:41,480
They eat so much.

116
00:04:41,481 --> 00:04:42,681
(They go through eight bags
of this a day.)

117
00:04:45,152 --> 00:04:48,087
I thought they came to wake us up.
Did they just come for breakfast?

118
00:04:48,555 --> 00:04:50,723
This isn't a wake-up call.

119
00:04:51,425 --> 00:04:53,693
- It's a breakfast buffet.
- Just morning feeding time.

120
00:04:55,629 --> 00:04:56,562
By the way,

121
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:58,931
I noticed something while feeding them.

122
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:00,700
Their eyes soften up when they eat.

123
00:05:00,701 --> 00:05:02,234
- A little bit, yeah.
- Right?

124
00:05:02,235 --> 00:05:03,469
They've got a food coma coming on.

125
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,370
They're slowing down.

126
00:05:04,371 --> 00:05:05,237
Totally.

127
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,374
She's leaving.

128
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:08,842
She's over it now.

129
00:05:09,043 --> 00:05:10,443
(Turning around)

130
00:05:10,444 --> 00:05:11,310
All done?

131
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,144
(Turning around completely full)

132
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,283
What if she poops right now?

133
00:05:18,785 --> 00:05:19,885
Diarrhea?

134
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:22,621
The grandma turned around.

135
00:05:22,622 --> 00:05:23,622
She's walking off.

136
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:25,391
- They turned around so many times.
- I know.

137
00:05:25,392 --> 00:05:27,426
(Nervous)

138
00:05:27,427 --> 00:05:28,327
(Suspicious noise)

139
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,795
Wait. What was that?

140
00:05:29,796 --> 00:05:30,763
(Farting)

141
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:33,198
(Wake up!)

142
00:05:33,199 --> 00:05:34,366
- I'm scared.
- Was that a fart?

143
00:05:34,367 --> 00:05:35,701
(The post-breakfast wake-up blast)

144
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:37,703
- It stinks.
- I can totally smell it!

145
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:39,238
She farted!

146
00:05:39,707 --> 00:05:40,740
She really just farted.

147
00:05:40,741 --> 00:05:41,807
Cover her butt.

148
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:43,743
- What?
- Block her butt!

149
00:05:43,978 --> 00:05:45,878
We're way too close!

150
00:05:45,879 --> 00:05:47,213
(A face-to-face wake-up call)

151
00:05:47,214 --> 00:05:49,382
- That was right in our faces.
- She was way too close.

152
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:52,785
Are you going to poop here too?

153
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,587
Are you seriously doing this?

154
00:05:54,955 --> 00:05:55,955
Hold it in.

155
00:05:55,956 --> 00:05:57,156
(Thankfully, the wake-up call
ends safely.)

156
00:05:57,524 --> 00:05:58,757
Girls.

157
00:05:58,925 --> 00:06:01,927
Thanks for stopping by to wake us up!

158
00:06:01,928 --> 00:06:04,296
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

159
00:06:04,964 --> 00:06:06,398
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

160
00:06:07,267 --> 00:06:09,401
- Bye!
- They're so sweet.

161
00:06:09,402 --> 00:06:11,170
Bye-bye!

162
00:06:11,195 --> 00:06:13,062
Just pretending to say goodbye...

163
00:06:13,476 --> 00:06:14,777
While acting like they're being polite.

164
00:06:14,809 --> 00:06:15,941
They aren't leaving!

165
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:18,310
Should we ask the handler
to take a picture of us?

166
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:19,745
Sounds good.

167
00:06:19,846 --> 00:06:22,080
One, two, three.

168
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:27,286
- Thank you!
- Thank you so much!

169
00:06:27,663 --> 00:06:30,098
- Bye.
- Bye.

170
00:06:30,123 --> 00:06:31,957
See you again!

171
00:06:31,958 --> 00:06:33,460
I've already gotten attached.

172
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:36,562
- My first-ever elephant wake-up call.
- An elephant wake-up call!

173
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:37,897
(The elephant wake-up call
definitely did its job.)

174
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,598
- That was so much fun.
- It totally woke me up.

175
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:43,836
Elephants!

176
00:06:43,837 --> 00:06:45,938
The only downside
to an elephant wake-up call,

177
00:06:45,939 --> 00:06:47,172
dirty hands.

178
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,473
(Filthy)

179
00:06:48,474 --> 00:06:50,309
Watching them eat made me hungry.

180
00:06:50,679 --> 00:06:51,611
- I'm starving.
- Me too.

181
00:06:51,612 --> 00:06:52,646
- You're hungry, right?
- Totally.

182
00:06:52,647 --> 00:06:54,913
I could go for an omelet and some coffee.

183
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,082
I hope they have that here.

184
00:06:56,517 --> 00:06:59,117
Let's wash our hands first.
Our schedule is pretty light today anyway.

185
00:06:59,319 --> 00:07:01,420
Let's figure out what we want to do.

186
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:02,956
Actually, there is one thing
I really want to do today.

187
00:07:03,623 --> 00:07:05,090
- I...
- I...

188
00:07:05,192 --> 00:07:06,125
want...

189
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,295
to make today a total dress-up day!

190
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,162
- Oh, sounds fun.
- Princess Day?

191
00:07:10,163 --> 00:07:11,797
- Princess Day?
- Love that.

192
00:07:12,399 --> 00:07:13,499
Are you down?

193
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,467
Totally.

194
00:07:14,468 --> 00:07:16,235
(Won Ji, you're the best.)

195
00:07:16,236 --> 00:07:18,504
We've never really
dressed up on our trips.

196
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:20,373
I really want to get all dolled up today.

197
00:07:20,841 --> 00:07:22,942
It's been forever since we all dressed up.

198
00:07:22,943 --> 00:07:25,412
Are you up for trying traditional outfits?

199
00:07:25,413 --> 00:07:28,281
I've never tried
on traditional Thai clothes before.

200
00:07:28,282 --> 00:07:29,648
Me neither.

201
00:07:29,649 --> 00:07:31,951
Let's go for it.

202
00:07:32,018 --> 00:07:33,318
And let's hit a great noodle spot.

203
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:35,654
- Your go-to place.
- My absolute favorite noodle spot.

204
00:07:35,655 --> 00:07:36,855
We're going.

205
00:07:37,057 --> 00:07:38,146
I got a smudge on my shirt.

206
00:07:38,170 --> 00:07:39,736
One of the trunks must have
brushed against it.

207
00:07:39,761 --> 00:07:41,493
I need to wash this today.

208
00:07:41,494 --> 00:07:42,728
We should definitely do laundry today.

209
00:07:42,729 --> 00:07:44,096
- Let's do laundry.
- Definitely.

210
00:07:44,097 --> 00:07:45,865
Come to think of it,
we need to take care of that too.

211
00:07:45,866 --> 00:07:46,732
Let's handle that first.

212
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:49,535
- Let's roll!
- Let's go.

213
00:07:50,103 --> 00:07:51,136
Let's go.

214
00:07:52,339 --> 00:07:54,206
The weather is gorgeous.

215
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:55,207
(One hour later, lodge)

216
00:07:55,208 --> 00:07:56,876
Look at how blue the sky is.

217
00:08:03,617 --> 00:08:07,086
(Unbelievable!)

218
00:08:07,087 --> 00:08:08,388
Is there another elephant in our room?

219
00:08:09,256 --> 00:08:10,389
(An elephant-shaped dish)

220
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:12,858
- What is that?
- I'm scared.

221
00:08:12,859 --> 00:08:15,061
I'm getting nervous.

222
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:19,098
(Dopamine rush incoming)

223
00:08:19,099 --> 00:08:20,065
That's a QR code!

224
00:08:21,902 --> 00:08:23,169
Let's scan it.

225
00:08:24,271 --> 00:08:25,172
(Scanning the QR code)

226
00:08:25,173 --> 00:08:26,739
What does it say?

227
00:08:27,941 --> 00:08:28,841
(Gasps)

228
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,843
What's our third destination?

229
00:08:31,445 --> 00:08:32,955
"A jungle village called Bukit Lawang."

230
00:08:32,979 --> 00:08:34,246
Isn't this a jungle already?

231
00:08:34,247 --> 00:08:35,047
Where on earth is that?

232
00:08:35,448 --> 00:08:37,082
- "However..."
- "However?"

233
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:41,820
"You will not have your luggage with you
during your stay in the village."

234
00:08:42,389 --> 00:08:43,924
They'll give us a place to stay, right?

235
00:08:43,925 --> 00:08:45,791
Wait, it's in Indonesia!

236
00:08:45,792 --> 00:08:46,859
What?

237
00:08:47,627 --> 00:08:50,929
(Looking up Bukit Lawang)

238
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:53,298
"Bukit Lawang?"
I've never heard of it in my life.

239
00:08:53,299 --> 00:08:55,133
- Me neither.
- It doesn't ring a bell at all.

240
00:08:55,134 --> 00:08:56,835
(Even Won Ji has never heard of it.)

241
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:59,304
It's practically right on the equator!

242
00:09:00,473 --> 00:09:02,274
- Right on the equator!
- It's right there!

243
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:03,475
You're so right.

244
00:09:03,476 --> 00:09:05,110
- Right on the equator.
- It is going to be boiling!

245
00:09:05,111 --> 00:09:07,179
- Look at that!
- It's going to be scorching.

246
00:09:07,614 --> 00:09:08,480
See where the equator is?

247
00:09:08,481 --> 00:09:10,416
- That's the equator.
- It's going to be insanely hot.

248
00:09:10,417 --> 00:09:12,885
Are you guys actively
trying to torture me?

249
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:15,087
(Eyes widening)

250
00:09:15,422 --> 00:09:16,655
I'm so worried.

251
00:09:17,457 --> 00:09:19,992
What's the temperature over there?

252
00:09:21,328 --> 00:09:23,029
- It says 33 degrees Celsius.
- It's 33 degrees.

253
00:09:23,363 --> 00:09:25,597
And with the humidity,

254
00:09:25,865 --> 00:09:27,432
- it'll feel...
- Way hotter.

255
00:09:27,433 --> 00:09:28,667
way hotter.

256
00:09:28,668 --> 00:09:30,735
Wait, we really won't have
our luggage with us?

257
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:32,972
Then what are we supposed to travel with?

258
00:09:32,973 --> 00:09:34,507
Can we at least get a daypack?

259
00:09:34,508 --> 00:09:38,044
Are we expected to live
like monkeys out there?

260
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:40,562
We're literally going to become one
with the monkeys.

261
00:09:40,587 --> 00:09:42,681
At least we had AC here.

262
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:44,316
(Checking out
their upcoming accommodation)

263
00:09:44,317 --> 00:09:46,184
- Wow.
- Oh boy...

264
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:48,554
- That's a monkey!
- A real monkey!

265
00:09:48,555 --> 00:09:49,722
That is an actual monkey.

266
00:09:49,723 --> 00:09:51,490
Wait, isn't that a gorilla?

267
00:09:51,491 --> 00:09:52,324
Why is it so huge?

268
00:09:52,493 --> 00:09:54,693
Are we hanging out with monkeys this time?

269
00:09:55,896 --> 00:09:57,497
People are raving
about this place, though.

270
00:09:58,023 --> 00:09:59,744
"Orangutans, elephants, bats..."

271
00:09:59,776 --> 00:10:01,667
"I can't recommend
the wildlife tours enough."

272
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:03,754
They're totally wild orangutans.

273
00:10:03,767 --> 00:10:06,639
There are monkeys right along the road.

274
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,108
So cute!

275
00:10:11,077 --> 00:10:12,377
- Adorable!
- Look at that smile.

276
00:10:13,198 --> 00:10:14,678
I can't wait to see them.

277
00:10:15,525 --> 00:10:17,016
They're all jungle treks, though.

278
00:10:17,017 --> 00:10:18,185
- Listen up, everyone.
- Yes?

279
00:10:18,205 --> 00:10:20,138
We have an announcement.

280
00:10:20,158 --> 00:10:20,987
- Okay.
- What is it?

281
00:10:21,988 --> 00:10:25,925
Our flight today got canceled.

282
00:10:26,505 --> 00:10:27,827
- We can't go?
- Which means...

283
00:10:28,078 --> 00:10:30,964
we get to stay longer in Chiang Mai!

284
00:10:31,645 --> 00:10:36,352
You have free time to explore Chiang Mai
until this evening.

285
00:10:36,498 --> 00:10:38,171
- We get free time?
- Even better!

286
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:41,107
Then let's get all dolled up today!

287
00:10:41,132 --> 00:10:43,805
Let's take tons of photos
and wear pretty clothes.

288
00:10:43,806 --> 00:10:45,631
Let's do everything on our bucket list!

289
00:10:45,791 --> 00:10:47,914
- Let's sing and dance.
- Turn Won Ji into a princess.

290
00:10:48,448 --> 00:10:50,216
She's totally lost for words.

291
00:10:50,365 --> 00:10:52,538
Wait, shouldn't we check out first?

292
00:10:52,562 --> 00:10:53,653
Check it out.

293
00:10:53,696 --> 00:10:54,954
- Check it out.
- Let's check out.

294
00:10:55,076 --> 00:10:56,489
- We need to check out first.
- Right.

295
00:10:56,490 --> 00:10:58,858
Let's pack up, tidy the room,
and get going.

296
00:10:58,859 --> 00:10:59,659
Sounds good.

297
00:10:59,699 --> 00:11:01,413
If it's inevitable, just roll with it!

298
00:11:01,414 --> 00:11:02,595
Just enjoy the ride!

299
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,427
Let's get the laundry going first.

300
00:11:06,447 --> 00:11:08,801
- Laundry before we head out.
- Knock out a load before we go.

301
00:11:09,102 --> 00:11:10,937
We should wash everything we've worn.

302
00:11:11,674 --> 00:11:13,473
- This is dirty too.
- Start with this one.

303
00:11:14,928 --> 00:11:18,354
(Rocking the exact same outfits
from Day 1)

304
00:11:18,814 --> 00:11:21,781
(Abra-ca-Salon opens for Princess Day.)

305
00:11:22,188 --> 00:11:24,608
(Laser-focused)

306
00:11:26,174 --> 00:11:27,654
This is fun. You're so gentle.

307
00:11:29,389 --> 00:11:30,857
I honestly forgot how to do this.

308
00:11:31,304 --> 00:11:32,358
You forgot?

309
00:11:32,359 --> 00:11:34,359
- How to put on makeup.
- How to do your makeup?

310
00:11:35,345 --> 00:11:38,172
(The trip wiped out her makeup memory.)

311
00:11:39,112 --> 00:11:41,856
(Meanwhile, Won Ji hunts
for a laundromat.)

312
00:11:42,296 --> 00:11:43,603
There's barely anything to pack.

313
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:45,071
Seriously.

314
00:11:45,072 --> 00:11:47,076
(Packing complete)

315
00:11:47,816 --> 00:11:48,775
All set.

316
00:11:49,342 --> 00:11:51,711
You look gorgeous today!

317
00:11:52,061 --> 00:11:53,794
(Back to her fabulous self after so long)

318
00:11:53,795 --> 00:11:55,248
- Naturally!
- Looking stylish as ever.

319
00:11:56,287 --> 00:11:58,418
Let's double-check
that we didn't miss anything.

320
00:11:59,786 --> 00:12:02,755
Put the sandals in a plastic bag.

321
00:12:04,758 --> 00:12:05,632
(Stacking everything neatly)

322
00:12:07,545 --> 00:12:08,645
(Giving it a good squeeze)

323
00:12:09,278 --> 00:12:11,558
(Her packing skills
just keep leveling up.)

324
00:12:12,038 --> 00:12:13,199
Hold on a sec.

325
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:16,407
(Zipping it up like a pro)

326
00:12:16,439 --> 00:12:17,876
It closes with zero struggle.

327
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,205
It really does.

328
00:12:19,639 --> 00:12:20,607
Easy.

329
00:12:21,407 --> 00:12:22,375
Let's roll.

330
00:12:22,842 --> 00:12:24,143
Let's go.

331
00:12:24,711 --> 00:12:26,711
We're checking out.

332
00:12:28,314 --> 00:12:30,683
We had the best time! It was so much fun.

333
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:34,988
The elephants came to send us off!

334
00:12:35,321 --> 00:12:37,924
- They came to say goodbye!
- Hello!

335
00:12:38,281 --> 00:12:40,393
They're so precious.

336
00:12:41,261 --> 00:12:44,397
- Bye-bye!
- We have to get going now, guys.

337
00:12:44,864 --> 00:12:48,368
(The girls say their fond farewells.)

338
00:12:48,668 --> 00:12:50,975
- Too cute.
- They're so cute.

339
00:12:50,976 --> 00:12:52,472
He wants to shake on it!

340
00:12:55,527 --> 00:12:56,618
So adorable.

341
00:12:56,643 --> 00:12:59,121
Thank you so much. We had a blast.

342
00:12:59,141 --> 00:13:00,346
I've grown so attached.

343
00:13:01,688 --> 00:13:04,915
(One last affectionate embrace)

344
00:13:05,184 --> 00:13:06,552
We're heading out now. Bye!

345
00:13:06,648 --> 00:13:08,054
He really won't let go.

346
00:13:08,128 --> 00:13:10,423
- He must really love you.
- He's hanging on tight.

347
00:13:10,795 --> 00:13:11,758
I really have to go.

348
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:14,761
(Clinging to her just like a baby elephant
wanting love)

349
00:13:14,775 --> 00:13:16,663
This is actually so sad.

350
00:13:16,664 --> 00:13:18,230
(Tearing up)

351
00:13:18,409 --> 00:13:20,409
- So precious.
- Right?

352
00:13:20,410 --> 00:13:21,367
He finally let go.

353
00:13:21,537 --> 00:13:22,802
- Bye!
- Take care!

354
00:13:23,169 --> 00:13:25,305
(Time for the real goodbye)

355
00:13:26,773 --> 00:13:29,342
- Is he crying?
- Oh no, why?

356
00:13:30,199 --> 00:13:31,311
We're taking off now.

357
00:13:31,312 --> 00:13:32,979
(Heartbroken,
they stop in their tracks again.)

358
00:13:33,773 --> 00:13:35,048
Bye!

359
00:13:37,646 --> 00:13:39,919
Thank you!

360
00:13:39,959 --> 00:13:42,322
Was he waving goodbye?

361
00:13:43,256 --> 00:13:45,692
- Elephants are brilliant.
- They really are incredibly smart.

362
00:13:45,803 --> 00:13:47,226
You'll remember us, right?

363
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:51,064
- Wave goodbye.
- Bye.

364
00:13:51,065 --> 00:13:52,481
(Suddenly reaching out with its trunk)

365
00:13:52,658 --> 00:13:54,100
Give me a hug!

366
00:13:54,101 --> 00:13:55,998
(A big, warm hug)

367
00:13:56,051 --> 00:13:57,070
He hugged her!

368
00:13:57,225 --> 00:13:58,338
Finally!

369
00:13:58,339 --> 00:14:03,019
(A deep bond formed
just as they part ways)

370
00:14:03,020 --> 00:14:03,776
I'm leaving now.

371
00:14:03,885 --> 00:14:05,144
Bye!

372
00:14:05,678 --> 00:14:07,480
Goodbye.

373
00:14:07,659 --> 00:14:09,659
- Bye-bye, elephant!
- Bye-bye!

374
00:14:10,149 --> 00:14:12,149
(Safe travels, take care.)

375
00:14:12,552 --> 00:14:15,254
- Let's go.
- We have to cross this bridge again.

376
00:14:15,261 --> 00:14:16,977
(The four press on,
bittersweet smiles all around.)

377
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:18,458
I truly loved this place.

378
00:14:18,503 --> 00:14:20,893
Is it just me, or does this feel tougher
the further we get?

379
00:14:20,910 --> 00:14:22,462
I know what you mean.

380
00:14:22,795 --> 00:14:23,863
Let's go check out.

381
00:14:24,330 --> 00:14:26,330
- Okay.
- I'm so bummed to leave.

382
00:14:26,772 --> 00:14:29,441
Could you call us a taxi into town?

383
00:14:29,701 --> 00:14:30,803
- Okay.
- All set?

384
00:14:30,915 --> 00:14:33,406
Sure thing, I'll call one for you.

385
00:14:33,435 --> 00:14:35,006
How long will it take?

386
00:14:35,187 --> 00:14:37,439
Around 5 to 10 minutes.

387
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,888
- Thanks!
- It'll be here in no time.

388
00:14:38,913 --> 00:14:40,146
We'll wait out front.

389
00:14:40,253 --> 00:14:42,315
- Sounds good.
- Thank you so much!

390
00:14:42,347 --> 00:14:44,183
- Sawasdee khap.
- Khop khun ka.

391
00:14:44,184 --> 00:14:46,352
(Khop khun ka.)

392
00:14:46,558 --> 00:14:48,851
She said about 5 to 10 minutes.

393
00:14:48,852 --> 00:14:50,490
- It should pull up soon.
- Yeah.

394
00:14:51,264 --> 00:14:52,725
It's another scorcher today.

395
00:14:53,419 --> 00:14:55,399
(The sun beats down relentlessly
once again.)

396
00:14:55,612 --> 00:14:56,429
It's blazing hot.

397
00:14:56,430 --> 00:14:58,430
Want to put on sunscreen while we wait?

398
00:14:58,431 --> 00:14:59,232
Good idea.

399
00:14:59,251 --> 00:15:00,500
- The sun is brutal.
- Tell me about it.

400
00:15:00,651 --> 00:15:01,894
My skin is about to peel.

401
00:15:01,895 --> 00:15:03,151
You got burned pretty bad.

402
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,570
Here, let me put some on you.

403
00:15:04,779 --> 00:15:06,147
Lining up for my sunscreen ration.

404
00:15:06,172 --> 00:15:06,799
Thank you.

405
00:15:07,125 --> 00:15:10,279
(Sharing Lee Sian's sunscreen)

406
00:15:10,643 --> 00:15:12,278
Shower me with it!

407
00:15:12,699 --> 00:15:14,580
- Sunscreen shower.
- Careful there.

408
00:15:14,581 --> 00:15:16,416
Because it seriously stings.

409
00:15:16,955 --> 00:15:18,968
- Do our necks too.
- Don't miss the back.

410
00:15:20,035 --> 00:15:24,281
(Total UV defense in a single bottle)

411
00:15:24,421 --> 00:15:25,425
No sunburn for me today.

412
00:15:25,581 --> 00:15:26,492
Nice.

413
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:30,430
Let's make the most
of downtown Chiang Mai today.

414
00:15:30,454 --> 00:15:32,331
- Love that plan.
- I've been dying to check it out.

415
00:15:32,332 --> 00:15:33,533
We haven't been downtown yet.

416
00:15:33,534 --> 00:15:35,134
Are we hitting up that noodle place?

417
00:15:35,135 --> 00:15:36,869
We have to make time for it.

418
00:15:37,032 --> 00:15:39,307
- That spot is a must every time I visit.
- We're definitely going.

419
00:15:39,332 --> 00:15:40,440
Is that our cab?

420
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:41,607
Our taxi's here!

421
00:15:41,665 --> 00:15:42,642
- Let's go.
- Quick, quick.

422
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:47,313
- Let's roll.
- That was fast.

423
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,916
- Thank you!
- Sawasdee khap.

424
00:15:50,876 --> 00:15:51,818
Khop khun ka.

425
00:15:52,819 --> 00:15:54,387
We can toss the bags in the back.

426
00:15:55,223 --> 00:15:56,155
Tons of trunk space.

427
00:15:56,356 --> 00:15:58,356
- I don't mind taking the middle seat.
- No, you're fine.

428
00:15:58,357 --> 00:16:00,656
- Let's go.
- It's pretty roomy.

429
00:16:00,843 --> 00:16:02,128
- Khop khun ka.
- Bye!

430
00:16:03,329 --> 00:16:04,530
(Heading straight
into downtown Chiang Mai)

431
00:16:04,531 --> 00:16:06,132
- Short, but unforgettable.
- Truly.

432
00:16:06,133 --> 00:16:07,433
It was such an intense experience.

433
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:12,772
Look at that scenery. It's gorgeous.

434
00:16:12,790 --> 00:16:14,440
Right?

435
00:16:15,176 --> 00:16:17,176
- We really came up high.
- Totally.

436
00:16:17,177 --> 00:16:18,463
We climbed pretty far up.

437
00:16:18,464 --> 00:16:19,946
So we were up in the mountains
the whole time.

438
00:16:20,436 --> 00:16:22,048
You're right,
this is deep in the mountains.

439
00:16:22,049 --> 00:16:23,249
I had no idea.

440
00:16:23,463 --> 00:16:25,463
All right, I'll make us
some background music.

441
00:16:25,464 --> 00:16:26,352
Yes, please.

442
00:16:26,353 --> 00:16:28,343
- Our resident maestro.
- I've already made...

443
00:16:28,368 --> 00:16:29,722
around ten songs.

444
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:31,290
It only takes a second.

445
00:16:32,151 --> 00:16:33,328
I pumped out a ton yesterday.

446
00:16:33,353 --> 00:16:34,927
"Abra-ca-Empty" is such a catchy name.

447
00:16:34,928 --> 00:16:36,496
I love it too.

448
00:16:36,542 --> 00:16:38,898
We could use a fresh theme song.

449
00:16:38,899 --> 00:16:39,848
Right?

450
00:16:40,228 --> 00:16:43,135
(Whenever she had a free second)

451
00:16:43,468 --> 00:16:45,641
(Gabee was in the lab
cooking up theme songs)

452
00:16:46,361 --> 00:16:48,894
(Fully hooked on AI songwriting)

453
00:16:49,342 --> 00:16:52,267
Do you actually make
real music with that app?

454
00:16:52,307 --> 00:16:52,979
No way.

455
00:16:53,154 --> 00:16:55,373
- Just for fun?
- Totally just for laughs.

456
00:16:55,374 --> 00:16:58,251
Mostly when I'm just
messing around with friends.

457
00:16:59,018 --> 00:17:01,053
I heard a snippet earlier,
and it was actually fire.

458
00:17:01,054 --> 00:17:03,507
I'll play all the tracks
I've cooked up so far.

459
00:17:03,531 --> 00:17:04,724
- Hit it.
- Hit it.

460
00:17:04,781 --> 00:17:06,792
Time to hear the Gabee discography.

461
00:17:06,874 --> 00:17:10,029
- First up, the Arabian vibes.
- Arabian style.

462
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:12,031
An addictive Arabic groove.

463
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:15,968
That intro is killer.

464
00:17:16,143 --> 00:17:18,437
<i>Abra-ca-Empty, Abra-ca-Empty</i>

465
00:17:18,623 --> 00:17:20,973
<i>Keep it or toss it, what's it going to be?</i>

466
00:17:21,209 --> 00:17:23,442
<i>When in doubt, throw it out</i>

467
00:17:23,643 --> 00:17:25,470
(The lyrics hit surprisingly
close to home.)

468
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:27,510
<i>That's just life</i>

469
00:17:27,643 --> 00:17:29,183
I love this.

470
00:17:29,184 --> 00:17:30,182
- Catchy, right?
- Totally.

471
00:17:30,203 --> 00:17:32,418
Next, I tried a K-pop vibe.

472
00:17:32,419 --> 00:17:33,419
- Nice!
- K-pop style.

473
00:17:34,259 --> 00:17:35,755
<i>Abra-ca-Empty</i>

474
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:39,016
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty</i>
- Wait, that sounds so familiar!

475
00:17:39,062 --> 00:17:40,426
It really does sound familiar.

476
00:17:41,955 --> 00:17:44,956
(Familiar melodies hit the hardest)

477
00:17:45,142 --> 00:17:48,629
<i>- Empty it out, throw it out, clean it out
- Empty it out</i>

478
00:17:48,796 --> 00:17:50,143
<i>Lighten, lighten, lighten the load</i>

479
00:17:50,176 --> 00:17:52,071
<i>Lighten every single load</i>

480
00:17:54,069 --> 00:17:59,300
Look, the driver was
tapping along to the beat.

481
00:17:59,301 --> 00:18:01,180
- She was totally vibing.
- This is the one.

482
00:18:01,454 --> 00:18:04,480
Every single hook gets stuck in your head.

483
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,500
And by Won Ji's special request,

484
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,888
- I whipped up a hip-hop version.
- Hip-hop was my idea.

485
00:18:09,618 --> 00:18:13,325
(The hip-hop version drops.)

486
00:18:13,326 --> 00:18:14,460
Total Y2K vibes!

487
00:18:16,202 --> 00:18:18,998
Why does this slap so hard?

488
00:18:19,858 --> 00:18:22,452
<i>Luggage, luggage, luggage, luggage,
Abra-ca-Empty</i>

489
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:23,384
<i>Empty it out, empty it out</i>

490
00:18:23,409 --> 00:18:24,670
<i>Clear everything out</i>

491
00:18:25,198 --> 00:18:27,745
<i>Lighten, lighten, lighten,
lighten every load</i>

492
00:18:27,818 --> 00:18:29,775
- Hip-hop never misses.
- This is so good.

493
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:31,310
I'm obsessed with this hip-hop track.

494
00:18:31,690 --> 00:18:34,580
Addictive beats are just unbeatable,
aren't they?

495
00:18:34,581 --> 00:18:35,348
For real.

496
00:18:35,349 --> 00:18:37,200
It needs that old-school
trot bounce, though.

497
00:18:37,201 --> 00:18:39,201
Should we drop a trot version too?

498
00:18:39,202 --> 00:18:40,109
Trot would be iconic.

499
00:18:40,110 --> 00:18:41,487
Let me whip up a trot remix.

500
00:18:41,488 --> 00:18:42,922
- I'm so hyped for the trot.
- Let's go.

501
00:18:43,035 --> 00:18:45,035
Give me a second to punch in the prompt.

502
00:18:45,036 --> 00:18:46,759
(The maestro works her magic.)

503
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:49,762
All three are great, but the hip-hop one
is surprisingly catchy.

504
00:18:50,209 --> 00:18:52,431
"Abra-ca-Empty, Abra-ca-Empty,"

505
00:18:52,698 --> 00:18:54,609
"I'll lighten your load."

506
00:18:54,610 --> 00:18:55,497
Can we use that line?

507
00:18:55,498 --> 00:18:57,603
That's pure trot material.

508
00:18:57,691 --> 00:18:59,305
Love that lyric.

509
00:18:59,306 --> 00:19:00,473
- Perfect, right?
- Yeah.

510
00:19:00,544 --> 00:19:04,210
Toss in some vocal trills
and a gritty vibrato.

511
00:19:04,277 --> 00:19:06,379
<i>No matter what comes, no matter what!</i>

512
00:19:06,445 --> 00:19:07,513
Just like that.

513
00:19:07,973 --> 00:19:09,893
(Generated in a flash)

514
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:13,660
(Track 4: The Trot Version)

515
00:19:14,213 --> 00:19:16,328
<i>I'll lighten your load</i>

516
00:19:16,353 --> 00:19:17,056
It's good.

517
00:19:17,589 --> 00:19:20,359
<i>Abra-ca-Empty, Abra-ca-Empty</i>

518
00:19:20,612 --> 00:19:22,161
<i>Luggage, luggage, luggage, luggage</i>

519
00:19:22,205 --> 00:19:24,205
<i>Abra-ca-Empty</i>

520
00:19:24,232 --> 00:19:25,498
Now this is good!

521
00:19:25,899 --> 00:19:27,416
(Bouncing along to the rhythm)

522
00:19:27,443 --> 00:19:29,089
<i>Empty it out, empty it out</i>

523
00:19:29,143 --> 00:19:31,671
<i>Clear everything out</i>

524
00:19:34,230 --> 00:19:36,442
<i>Lighten, lighten, lighten</i>

525
00:19:36,483 --> 00:19:39,014
<i>Lighten every single load</i>

526
