I'll go with chicken.

1581
00:58:27,670 --> 00:58:30,440
- Water spinach for the last time?
- Sounds good.

1582
00:58:30,477 --> 00:58:31,608
Okay.

1583
00:58:31,609 --> 00:58:33,176
We order water spinach.

1584
00:58:33,329 --> 00:58:34,378
Excuse me.

1585
00:58:35,379 --> 00:58:37,681
Three beef and one chicken.

1586
00:58:37,722 --> 00:58:39,249
One water spinach.

1587
00:58:39,616 --> 00:58:41,184
No water spinach?

1588
00:58:41,196 --> 00:58:43,120
How about one spring roll?

1589
00:58:43,255 --> 00:58:45,355
- This.
- One spring roll.

1590
00:58:45,468 --> 00:58:47,624
One passion fruit juice, please.

1591
00:58:47,942 --> 00:58:49,092
Thank you.

1592
00:58:49,202 --> 00:58:50,994
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1593
00:58:52,295 --> 00:58:53,296
It must be good.

1594
00:58:53,349 --> 00:58:54,664
Let's eat and eat.

1595
00:58:55,932 --> 00:58:58,902
We really made the most of today.

1596
00:58:58,903 --> 00:59:00,133
We really did.

1597
00:59:00,134 --> 00:59:02,182
(Feeding elephants, making a song
and photo shoot)

1598
00:59:03,269 --> 00:59:05,342
(Is she losing her mind?)

1599
00:59:06,136 --> 00:59:09,029
(Drinking straight from the bottle)

1600
00:59:09,189 --> 00:59:10,747
- Are we losing our minds?
- Yes.

1601
00:59:12,416 --> 00:59:14,416
Passion fruit juice.

1602
00:59:14,642 --> 00:59:16,594
- That looks plump.
- It looks pretty.

1603
00:59:16,627 --> 00:59:18,902
(Passion fruit juice is served
in a pretty bowl.)

1604
00:59:22,238 --> 00:59:22,826
How is it?

1605
00:59:22,827 --> 00:59:23,860
- Is it good?
- Full of vitamins.

1606
00:59:24,318 --> 00:59:25,815
- Vitamins?
- I want some too.

1607
00:59:28,692 --> 00:59:29,119
(Clapping)

1608
00:59:29,633 --> 00:59:30,901
That's totally my kind of juice.

1609
00:59:34,026 --> 00:59:34,932
- Isn't it delicious?
- Yes.

1610
00:59:34,933 --> 00:59:35,972
- Do you want to share one with me?
- Yes.

1611
00:59:36,972 --> 00:59:38,732
(Excited)

1612
00:59:39,318 --> 00:59:40,872
Come on!

1613
00:59:40,979 --> 00:59:42,979
Excuse me. We want to order something.

1614
00:59:43,613 --> 00:59:45,048
- That one is so good.
- Isn't it?

1615
00:59:45,184 --> 00:59:47,617
- Your eyes went wide.
- Totally.

1616
00:59:47,618 --> 00:59:48,430
(It was so refreshing.)

1617
00:59:48,717 --> 00:59:50,490
- Here it is.
- Finally!

1618
00:59:50,710 --> 00:59:52,304
(The main dish, khao soi, is served.)

1619
00:59:54,697 --> 00:59:55,759
It looks good.

1620
00:59:55,760 --> 00:59:57,988
(Beef khao soi)

1621
00:59:58,628 --> 01:00:02,064
(Chicken khao soi)

1622
01:00:02,566 --> 01:00:05,568
(The spring rolls they will share)

1623
01:00:05,836 --> 01:00:08,237
It looks like egg noodles.

1624
01:00:08,638 --> 01:00:10,172
The noodles are
kind of like kalguksu noodles,

1625
01:00:10,173 --> 01:00:11,941
- but I think it's yellow because of eggs.
- Yes.

1626
01:00:11,942 --> 01:00:13,142
It looks like kalguksu.

1627
01:00:13,143 --> 01:00:14,810
Or maybe tofu noodles.

1628
01:00:15,512 --> 01:00:17,913
I don't know what this fried thing is.

1629
01:00:19,916 --> 01:00:20,916
It's nutty.

1630
01:00:21,619 --> 01:00:23,519
I think they fried the noodles.

1631
01:00:23,520 --> 01:00:24,687
(Crispy fried noodles
on top of boiled noodles)

1632
01:00:24,688 --> 01:00:25,488
It looks the same.

1633
01:00:27,057 --> 01:00:27,923
These are the noodles.

1634
01:00:28,992 --> 01:00:29,925
Here are the noodles,

1635
01:00:30,060 --> 01:00:32,261
and these on top are fried.

1636
01:00:32,262 --> 01:00:33,395
You're right.

1637
01:00:33,396 --> 01:00:34,396
They're so crispy.

1638
01:00:38,769 --> 01:00:41,371
(That face says it all.)

1639
01:00:41,605 --> 01:00:43,439
It has a little kick.

1640
01:00:43,941 --> 01:00:46,409
Koreans would love this, don't you think?

1641
01:00:46,643 --> 01:00:48,344
It's a spicy type of curry.

1642
01:00:48,345 --> 01:00:50,913
(Nutty coconut curry with a subtle kick)

1643
01:00:51,314 --> 01:00:54,916
I'm having the boiled noodles
with the fried ones together.

1644
01:00:55,652 --> 01:00:57,953
(Slurping)

1645
01:00:59,656 --> 01:01:01,223
Can you try the chicken legs too?

1646
01:01:02,993 --> 01:01:04,193
(One fierce queen)

1647
01:01:04,194 --> 01:01:06,262
- You're really enjoying that!
- And some soup.

1648
01:01:07,531 --> 01:01:10,099
(Washing it down with some soup)

1649
01:01:10,100 --> 01:01:11,100
It's so good.

1650
01:01:11,502 --> 01:01:14,370
It's crispy, chewy, spicy,
all in one bite.

1651
01:01:14,371 --> 01:01:15,204
Right.

1652
01:01:15,205 --> 01:01:16,472
(Khao soi nails both texture and flavor.)

1653
01:01:19,609 --> 01:01:21,210
(Yum!)

1654
01:01:21,311 --> 01:01:22,211
It's so good.

1655
01:01:27,418 --> 01:01:29,118
It's doing the meat justice.

1656
01:01:29,119 --> 01:01:29,819
(Thick)

1657
01:01:29,820 --> 01:01:31,487
Look at how thick it is.

1658
01:01:34,858 --> 01:01:36,559
The meat is so tender.

1659
01:01:37,227 --> 01:01:38,661
It's insane. The meat tastes amazing.

1660
01:01:38,662 --> 01:01:41,430
Doesn't it taste
like really tender marinated ribs?

1661
01:01:42,165 --> 01:01:43,432
It's delicious.

1662
01:01:45,902 --> 01:01:51,707
(Everyone is enjoying their food.)

1663
01:01:52,175 --> 01:01:55,244
(Fiddling)

1664
01:01:57,581 --> 01:01:59,649
I have a confession to make.

1665
01:02:00,317 --> 01:02:03,019
Curry is the one thing I don't eat.

1666
01:02:03,020 --> 01:02:04,720
Really?

1667
01:02:04,721 --> 01:02:07,590
But this could taste different,
so I'm giving it a go.

1668
01:02:07,692 --> 01:02:09,691
Curry is the one thing you can't eat?

1669
01:02:09,692 --> 01:02:11,059
I don't eat it.

1670
01:02:11,060 --> 01:02:12,394
- Why? Does it taste weird?
- Try it.

1671
01:02:12,395 --> 01:02:14,429
I don't really like the taste of curry.

1672
01:02:15,165 --> 01:02:16,398
But I'll try this.

1673
01:02:17,634 --> 01:02:21,371
(Trying Thai curry for the first time)

1674
01:02:21,372 --> 01:02:22,471
It's insanely good.

1675
01:02:25,675 --> 01:02:26,808
(Yum!)

1676
01:02:26,809 --> 01:02:28,110
(Loving it)

1677
01:02:29,145 --> 01:02:30,412
- Do you like it?
- It has a kick.

1678
01:02:31,047 --> 01:02:31,880
I like it.

1679
01:02:32,616 --> 01:02:35,318
(She's going in for another bite.)

1680
01:02:35,585 --> 01:02:37,152
(So good!)

1681
01:02:37,654 --> 01:02:39,321
Thai food is insane.

1682
01:02:39,322 --> 01:02:40,489
I can't believe today's the last day.

1683
01:02:42,225 --> 01:02:43,092
I love it.

1684
01:02:43,360 --> 01:02:45,328
You know I love crispy food, right?

1685
01:02:45,629 --> 01:02:46,329
(Nibbling)

1686
01:02:46,330 --> 01:02:49,798
You can eat all kinds
of Thai food now, Sian.

1687
01:02:49,799 --> 01:02:51,634
Am I actually into Thai food now?

1688
01:02:51,635 --> 01:02:53,436
- I know, right?
- It's actually ridiculous.

1689
01:02:53,437 --> 01:02:55,071
You're a Thai food master now.

1690
01:02:55,072 --> 01:02:56,138
So ridiculous.

1691
01:02:57,174 --> 01:02:58,741
I'm a die-hard on Team Korean food,

1692
01:02:59,342 --> 01:03:01,009
but I didn't ask for Korean food once.

1693
01:03:01,010 --> 01:03:02,010
You're right.

1694
01:03:03,046 --> 01:03:04,780
It makes you forget about Korean food.

1695
01:03:04,781 --> 01:03:05,681
(All officially Team Thai Food)

1696
01:03:05,682 --> 01:03:06,548
It's so good.

1697
01:03:06,616 --> 01:03:08,550
Try the chicken legs too.

1698
01:03:10,720 --> 01:03:11,820
Spring rolls.

1699
01:03:11,821 --> 01:03:12,988
(Dipping it in sauce)

1700
01:03:13,190 --> 01:03:15,525
You really love the sauce, don't you?

1701
01:03:19,162 --> 01:03:19,995
It's so good.

1702
01:03:21,698 --> 01:03:24,099
They really know how to season
these salads.

1703
01:03:24,100 --> 01:03:24,900
(Every dish was a hit.)

1704
01:03:24,901 --> 01:03:26,001
Why is it so good?

1705
01:03:26,002 --> 01:03:26,902
Peas?

1706
01:03:27,871 --> 01:03:31,874
What stuck with you guys the most
from this trip?

1707
01:03:32,075 --> 01:03:33,142
Let's each pick one.

1708
01:03:34,311 --> 01:03:36,845
I was so happy bathing the elephants.

1709
01:03:36,846 --> 01:03:37,646
Me too.

1710
01:03:37,647 --> 01:03:39,147
You really looked happy.

1711
01:03:39,783 --> 01:03:41,717
- Right.
- So happy.

1712
01:03:41,851 --> 01:03:45,220
If I had to choose one,
it would go with the elephants too.

1713
01:03:45,356 --> 01:03:46,822
When the elephant hugged me.

1714
01:03:46,924 --> 01:03:47,790
Right.

1715
01:03:47,791 --> 01:03:49,925
She hugged Gabee first.

1716
01:03:49,926 --> 01:03:50,793
(Gabee's pick: Elephant hug)

1717
01:03:50,794 --> 01:03:51,794
Even this morning,

1718
01:03:52,108 --> 01:03:53,161
she didn't let go of you.

1719
01:03:53,162 --> 01:03:54,529
I think she really liked you.

1720
01:03:54,732 --> 01:03:56,499
For me, it was when we had
that smoothie...

1721
01:03:56,933 --> 01:03:58,767
after getting soaked in the rain.

1722
01:03:58,768 --> 01:03:59,902
(The smoothie after the cave hike)

1723
01:03:59,903 --> 01:04:00,936
When we were soaked.

1724
01:04:01,605 --> 01:04:03,539
For me, it's probably...

1725
01:04:04,041 --> 01:04:05,707
when I first touched the elephant.

1726
01:04:06,643 --> 01:04:07,710
That was so funny.

1727
01:04:10,413 --> 01:04:13,248
But the horror experience was
definitely the most memorable.

1728
01:04:13,451 --> 01:04:14,450
- I totally agree.
- Yes.

1729
01:04:14,451 --> 01:04:15,417
(Instantly agreeing)

1730
01:04:15,585 --> 01:04:18,153
I think that's when we really bonded.

1731
01:04:18,288 --> 01:04:19,054
Totally.

1732
01:04:19,155 --> 01:04:19,955
We even linked arms.

1733
01:04:19,956 --> 01:04:21,156
We were relying on each other.

1734
01:04:21,658 --> 01:04:23,959
Maybe it's because of all the activities,
but time really flies.

1735
01:04:23,960 --> 01:04:24,893
Exactly.

1736
01:04:24,961 --> 01:04:27,596
We did this whole trip with one suitcase.

1737
01:04:28,198 --> 01:04:30,799
Was anything different
from what you expected?

1738
01:04:31,467 --> 01:04:32,801
There was way more room...

1739
01:04:33,370 --> 01:04:34,370
than I expected.

1740
01:04:34,804 --> 01:04:36,538
It really wasn't that hard.

1741
01:04:36,539 --> 01:04:38,106
I thought it'd be impossible.

1742
01:04:38,475 --> 01:04:39,975
Everything fits in it...

1743
01:04:40,510 --> 01:04:41,610
so well.

1744
01:04:41,611 --> 01:04:44,179
Packing the suitcase isn't
even a challenge anymore.

1745
01:04:44,180 --> 01:04:45,881
It's a small challenge, I guess.

1746
01:04:45,882 --> 01:04:47,116
How so?

1747
01:04:47,117 --> 01:04:49,051
We didn't put our laundry in it yet.

1748
01:04:49,052 --> 01:04:50,686
You're right.

1749
01:04:50,920 --> 01:04:53,688
Maybe that'll make it
a little challenging.

1750
01:04:53,857 --> 01:04:55,891
When we go to Indonesia,

1751
01:04:56,459 --> 01:04:58,960
will we get some glam time there too?

1752
01:04:59,095 --> 01:05:01,196
I think we'd look amazing there.

1753
01:05:01,531 --> 01:05:03,632
For me,

1754
01:05:04,001 --> 01:05:05,567
this was quite enough.

1755
01:05:07,270 --> 01:05:08,470
Was today the last time for you?

1756
01:05:08,972 --> 01:05:10,205
She totally means it.

1757
01:05:10,206 --> 01:05:13,108
You can tell by the look on her face.

1758
01:05:13,343 --> 01:05:14,744
To be honest,

1759
01:05:15,445 --> 01:05:18,147
I think I'd want to glam up even more
in a jungle.

1760
01:05:18,148 --> 01:05:19,348
- Wow.
- Are you for real?

1761
01:05:19,749 --> 01:05:21,850
I love the jungle outfit vibes.

1762
01:05:22,519 --> 01:05:25,721
I had to leave
most of my leopard print clothes behind...

1763
01:05:25,722 --> 01:05:26,889
to save space.

1764
01:05:27,023 --> 01:05:29,158
But in the jungle, it's a must.

1765
01:05:29,159 --> 01:05:30,559
- Great idea.
- Yes.

1766
01:05:30,760 --> 01:05:32,494
That's how you survive.

1767
01:05:32,495 --> 01:05:35,130
Otherwise, the leopards might target us.

1768
01:05:36,333 --> 01:05:37,199
That kind of makes sense.

1769
01:05:37,668 --> 01:05:40,503
I think we should go shopping
as soon as possible.

1770
01:05:40,504 --> 01:05:43,039
Let's do it quietly.

1771
01:05:44,074 --> 01:05:45,474
My belt is going to break soon.

1772
01:05:45,809 --> 01:05:46,675
It's so tight.

1773
01:05:46,676 --> 01:05:49,612
(Belt at its limit)

1774
01:05:49,813 --> 01:05:51,480
I couldn't finish this.

1775
01:05:51,948 --> 01:05:54,316
Exactly. That's actually insane.

1776
01:05:54,317 --> 01:05:55,751
You can usually eat two of those.

1777
01:05:55,752 --> 01:05:57,319
This is actually ridiculous.

1778
01:05:57,554 --> 01:06:00,756
It's so tight around my stomach.

1779
01:06:01,725 --> 01:06:03,125
Let's go get changed.

1780
01:06:03,326 --> 01:06:04,159
Yes.

1781
01:06:04,160 --> 01:06:05,961
- Let's take it off...
- And go for round two.

1782
01:06:06,996 --> 01:06:08,063
Great idea.

1783
01:06:09,466 --> 01:06:10,566
(Taking a bite)

1784
01:06:10,667 --> 01:06:12,101
Let's free our bodies.

1785
01:06:12,869 --> 01:06:14,269
I'd love to take it off,

1786
01:06:14,270 --> 01:06:16,071
but we'd be completely naked.

1787
01:06:16,239 --> 01:06:18,742
Let's go return these clothes.

1788
01:06:18,743 --> 01:06:19,675
Let's hurry.

1789
01:06:19,676 --> 01:06:21,009
Let's go.

1790
01:06:21,010 --> 01:06:22,244
I'm so full.

1791
01:06:23,414 --> 01:06:25,314
Thank you.

1792
01:06:25,315 --> 01:06:27,383
Thank you for the food.

1793
01:06:27,384 --> 01:06:29,164
(Khao soi: 560 baht,
spring rolls: 95 baht, drinks: 230 baht)

1794
01:06:29,165 --> 01:06:29,752
(Total: 8885 baht)

1795
01:06:29,919 --> 01:06:33,121
- Finally.
- Took long enough.

1796
01:06:33,490 --> 01:06:35,624
- My stomach is finally free.
- Yes.

1797
01:06:36,125 --> 01:06:37,692
Come to think of it,

1798
01:06:37,693 --> 01:06:39,294
we could've just done
the one-day course for our laundry.

1799
01:06:39,295 --> 01:06:40,195
I know, right?

1800
01:06:40,196 --> 01:06:42,464
We didn't need the three-hour express.

1801
01:06:42,465 --> 01:06:44,301
Look at us, splurging on express laundry.

1802
01:06:44,302 --> 01:06:46,268
Won Ji went full glam.

1803
01:06:46,436 --> 01:06:48,103
Now I have to hop on the plane like this.

1804
01:06:48,104 --> 01:06:48,971
You look great.

1805
01:06:48,972 --> 01:06:51,173
- Hello.
- Hello.

1806
01:06:51,174 --> 01:06:54,510
(Back to the laundromat)

1807
01:06:55,211 --> 01:06:57,746
- Pick up?
- Yes, pick up.

1808
01:06:57,747 --> 01:06:59,214
This one.

1809
01:07:00,083 --> 01:07:01,717
Thank you.

1810
01:07:01,718 --> 01:07:04,887
- They even organized it for us.
- Goodness.

1811
01:07:06,690 --> 01:07:07,956
- They folded everything.
- Wow.

1812
01:07:08,558 --> 01:07:10,159
- I'm touched.
- So touched.

1813
01:07:10,160 --> 01:07:11,026
I've never seen laundry...

1814
01:07:11,027 --> 01:07:13,962
- so neatly folded like this.
- This is amazing.

1815
01:07:14,130 --> 01:07:14,996
Our suitcase.

1816
01:07:15,765 --> 01:07:16,732
Okay.

1817
01:07:16,733 --> 01:07:18,333
(Reunited with our fifth member)

1818
01:07:18,334 --> 01:07:20,202
Okay, thank you.

1819
01:07:20,203 --> 01:07:21,837
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1820
01:07:21,838 --> 01:07:23,412
(Bowing)

1821
01:07:23,413 --> 01:07:26,608
(One last thank you in Thailand)

1822
01:07:26,709 --> 01:07:28,343
Let's head over there.

1823
01:07:29,045 --> 01:07:30,779
Let's go.

1824
01:07:30,847 --> 01:07:32,615
Chiang Mai was so much fun.

1825
01:07:32,616 --> 01:07:33,783
It was so fun.

1826
01:07:33,784 --> 01:07:35,951
We really made the most of it.

1827
01:07:35,952 --> 01:07:38,787
We really packed in all the good stuff.

1828
01:07:39,022 --> 01:07:41,056
Short but sweet. Next time,

1829
01:07:41,057 --> 01:07:42,158
it'd be fun to tour around this place.

1830
01:07:42,159 --> 01:07:44,326
It's a little sad we didn't get to.

1831
01:07:44,561 --> 01:07:47,897
No! It's so sad.
I wish we could stay longer.

1832
01:07:47,898 --> 01:07:48,931
The sunset is beautiful.

1833
01:07:48,932 --> 01:07:49,798
I know, right?

1834
01:07:49,799 --> 01:07:50,933
Chiang Mai!

1835
01:07:50,934 --> 01:07:53,002
- Today's sunset is insanely beautiful.
- It's purple.

1836
01:07:53,003 --> 01:07:54,336
(Even the sky makes it hard
to say goodbye.)

1837
01:07:54,337 --> 01:07:57,139
We also need to pack.

1838
01:07:57,140 --> 01:07:58,007
We need to pack our suitcase.

1839
01:07:58,008 --> 01:07:59,775
You're right.
Should we put in our laundry?

1840
01:08:00,109 --> 01:08:01,076
Yes, let's do that.

1841
01:08:01,077 --> 01:08:02,243
Right here?

1842
01:08:02,412 --> 01:08:04,046
Let's do it here.

1843
01:08:05,048 --> 01:08:06,748
We're putting in our laundry.

1844
01:08:06,749 --> 01:08:09,617
We have about five kilograms of laundry.

1845
01:08:11,154 --> 01:08:12,988
It's more packed than we thought.

1846
01:08:13,289 --> 01:08:14,589
That's true.

1847
01:08:14,590 --> 01:08:16,491
It's probably because of these shoes.

1848
01:08:16,693 --> 01:08:18,460
We could carry our shoes on the plane.

1849
01:08:18,461 --> 01:08:19,894
I'll carry these.

1850
01:08:19,895 --> 01:08:21,362
There's a lot in here.

1851
01:08:21,431 --> 01:08:22,731
Let's sit down first.

1852
01:08:22,732 --> 01:08:24,700
- Sit down.
- We need to fix this.

1853
01:08:24,934 --> 01:08:26,001
Let's sit.

1854
01:08:26,002 --> 01:08:27,702
- Let's do this.
- Let's distribute it.

1855
01:08:27,703 --> 01:08:29,104
Let's do it.

1856
01:08:29,105 --> 01:08:30,605
Gabee.

1857
01:08:31,307 --> 01:08:32,374
Thank you.

1858
01:08:32,375 --> 01:08:33,696
- Harimu.
- Yes.

1859
01:08:33,697 --> 01:08:35,751
(Putting things in their personal pouches
to create space)

1860
01:08:35,778 --> 01:08:38,213
For you, Sian. These are mine.

1861
01:08:38,214 --> 01:08:40,448
Two arm coolers.

1862
01:08:40,550 --> 01:08:41,583
And this.

1863
01:08:42,085 --> 01:08:43,452
A lot of these are mine.

1864
01:08:43,453 --> 01:08:45,220
- Guess you have a lot of clothes.
- Look at that.

1865
01:08:45,221 --> 01:08:47,122
Since when were you such a fashionista?

1866
01:08:47,123 --> 01:08:49,658
- You need to get rid of some.
- Won Ji has a lot of clothes.

1867
01:08:49,762 --> 01:08:51,060
There's one more.

1868
01:08:51,061 --> 01:08:52,328
This one's Gabee's.

1869
01:08:52,329 --> 01:08:53,195
When's mine coming?

1870
01:08:53,196 --> 01:08:54,530
Here you go finally.

1871
01:08:55,232 --> 01:08:56,698
Elephant, Ellie!

1872
01:08:56,699 --> 01:08:57,832
Sian barely has clothes.

1873
01:08:57,833 --> 01:08:59,134
Sian needs to buy some.

1874
01:08:59,135 --> 01:09:00,568
I really need to buy some.

1875
01:09:00,569 --> 01:09:01,970
(Simple)

1876
01:09:01,971 --> 01:09:04,372
Okay. Let's put them in now.

1877
01:09:04,541 --> 01:09:06,542
Wow, it actually fits.

1878
01:09:06,910 --> 01:09:10,112
So do we get money again
if we cut the weight?

1879
01:09:10,113 --> 01:09:11,146
(Extra spending money for weight lost)

1880
01:09:11,147 --> 01:09:12,948
I think we got
rid of at least one kilogram.

1881
01:09:12,949 --> 01:09:14,049
Let's see.

1882
01:09:14,050 --> 01:09:14,850
Okay.

1883
01:09:15,919 --> 01:09:16,752
Let's see.

1884
01:09:18,354 --> 01:09:19,154
(Human scale mode on)

1885
01:09:19,155 --> 01:09:20,822
Maybe it's around the same weight.

1886
01:09:23,126 --> 01:09:24,760
It's not 20. It's around 19.

1887
01:09:24,761 --> 01:09:26,028
Definitely.

1888
01:09:26,029 --> 01:09:26,929
Okay, let's go.

1889
01:09:26,930 --> 01:09:29,865
There's nothing more to take out now.

1890
01:09:29,866 --> 01:09:31,734
We only packed the bare minimum.

1891
01:09:31,834 --> 01:09:33,835
We checked each other's stuff,
and there's nothing left to cut.

1892
01:09:34,304 --> 01:09:35,804
- You sure about this?
- Yes.

1893
01:09:36,206 --> 01:09:37,973
You only get one chance now.

1894
01:09:38,141 --> 01:09:40,008
You're really pissing us off.

1895
01:09:40,009 --> 01:09:41,410
Why would you even say that?

1896
01:09:41,411 --> 01:09:42,277
(Playing hard to get first)

1897
01:09:42,278 --> 01:09:43,746
I don't like your attitude, sir.

1898
01:09:43,747 --> 01:09:44,546
Why?

1899
01:09:46,049 --> 01:09:47,082
How do you use this?

1900
01:09:47,083 --> 01:09:48,283
Same rules as before.

1901
01:09:48,284 --> 01:09:50,452
(The last weight recorded in Bangkok)

1902
01:09:50,453 --> 01:09:51,320
Ready?

1903
01:09:51,554 --> 01:09:54,823
(How much will the suitcase weigh?)

1904
01:09:55,124 --> 01:09:56,124
(Tapping)

1905
01:09:57,027 --> 01:09:58,360
Hold on.

1906
01:09:58,361 --> 01:09:59,761
- Give us a minute.
- Wait.

1907
01:09:59,762 --> 01:10:00,583
Wait a minute.

1908
01:10:00,617 --> 01:10:01,944
(Slowly backing away)

1909
01:10:02,004 --> 01:10:03,155
- Hold on.
- Hold on.

1910
01:10:03,199 --> 01:10:05,221
Let's each think
of just one thing to take out.

1911
01:10:05,288 --> 01:10:06,083
Hold on.

1912
01:10:06,084 --> 01:10:07,614
What are you doing?

1913
01:10:07,615 --> 01:10:09,027
(Brief meeting)

1914
01:10:09,221 --> 01:10:10,454
It was over the weight limit, right?

1915
01:10:10,494 --> 01:10:11,455
Just one.

1916
01:10:11,721 --> 01:10:14,575
Then let's each take out just one item
from our own stuff.

1917
01:10:14,600 --> 01:10:16,727
- I think...
- Let's take out at least one thing each.

1918
01:10:16,754 --> 01:10:17,561
I got it.

1919
01:10:17,928 --> 01:10:18,896
No matter what.

1920
01:10:18,897 --> 01:10:21,661
(Okay, let's do this properly now.)

1921
01:10:21,828 --> 01:10:23,721
This is my hat pouch.

1922
01:10:23,755 --> 01:10:25,135
Then just carry it on.

1923
01:10:25,536 --> 01:10:28,472
(Wear the bulky things
instead of packing them.)

1924
01:10:28,505 --> 01:10:30,055
Gabee, do you wear contacts?

1925
01:10:30,095 --> 01:10:30,974
No, I don't.

1926
01:10:31,575 --> 01:10:33,482
- Are you going to throw that away?
- Yes.

1927
01:10:33,582 --> 01:10:35,746
- Are you sure you'd throw away your life?
- Yes.

1928
01:10:36,046 --> 01:10:36,714
Why?

1929
01:10:36,873 --> 01:10:39,216
Also, I'll leave just one tube of glue.

1930
01:10:40,284 --> 01:10:42,453
This is a bombshell announcement.

1931
01:10:43,706 --> 01:10:46,093
(Harimu decides to give up
the excessive zipper bags.)

1932
01:10:46,193 --> 01:10:47,391
Well.

1933
01:10:49,246 --> 01:10:51,246
I really don't think
I'll need the curling iron.

1934
01:10:51,729 --> 01:10:52,996
Why did I even pack this?

1935
01:10:53,564 --> 01:10:55,332
I've never straightened my hair even once.

1936
01:10:55,333 --> 01:10:56,300
Not at all.

1937
01:10:56,850 --> 01:10:58,970
I'm definitely returning this.

1938
01:10:58,971 --> 01:11:00,189
(Gabee takes out her curling iron.)

1939
01:11:00,457 --> 01:11:01,672
Cosmetics.

1940
01:11:01,673 --> 01:11:03,006
(Sian also takes out her curling iron.)

1941
01:11:03,007 --> 01:11:03,974
Are you taking that out?

1942
01:11:03,975 --> 01:11:08,479
I think this is
probably the heaviest thing in my pouch.

1943
01:11:08,548 --> 01:11:11,382
But you kept saying you couldn't
give it up until the very end.

1944
01:11:11,383 --> 01:11:12,715
But I figured out a way.

1945
01:11:13,717 --> 01:11:16,987
If I don't use treatment,
my hair gets frizzy,

1946
01:11:17,454 --> 01:11:18,722
so it actually has more volume.

1947
01:11:18,788 --> 01:11:19,590
Is that so?

1948
01:11:19,591 --> 01:11:20,891
So I don't really need it.

1949
01:11:20,928 --> 01:11:21,859
Really?

1950
01:11:21,908 --> 01:11:23,127
I don't need it.

1951
01:11:23,494 --> 01:11:25,162
We're taking out the curling iron.

1952
01:11:25,163 --> 01:11:26,746
(Sian takes out her curling iron.)

1953
01:11:26,992 --> 01:11:30,434
The curling iron is the thing I've used
the least since coming here.

1954
01:11:30,868 --> 01:11:33,470
I thought I'd need it the most,

1955
01:11:33,837 --> 01:11:35,773
- but I haven't used it even once.
- Right.

1956
01:11:35,774 --> 01:11:36,940
I remember...

1957
01:11:36,941 --> 01:11:39,910
when we first packed our suitcases,
we had four hair irons.

1958
01:11:40,940 --> 01:11:42,160
- Seriously.
- Right.

1959
01:11:42,161 --> 01:11:43,473
We had some wide ones,

1960
01:11:43,513 --> 01:11:47,049
- Exactly.
- some flat ones, and everything.

1961
01:11:47,586 --> 01:11:50,492
But now we really don't need
hair irons at all.

1962
01:11:50,493 --> 01:11:52,122
- I haven't even touched one.
- Absolutely.

1963
01:11:52,186 --> 01:11:53,757
I didn't even plug it in.

1964
01:11:53,758 --> 01:11:54,746
(Zero hair irons on Day 5)

1965
01:11:54,959 --> 01:11:56,360
I'll return this.

1966
01:11:56,446 --> 01:11:57,961
I'm never going to wear it.

1967
01:11:58,164 --> 01:12:01,231
But I feel like there might be a time
when you need to wear even this.

1968
01:12:01,291 --> 01:12:02,099
No.

1969
01:12:02,204 --> 01:12:03,763
You really have nothing left to take out.

1970
01:12:03,784 --> 01:12:04,568
What is it?

1971
01:12:05,297 --> 01:12:06,957
(A brush they had forgotten about)

1972
01:12:07,017 --> 01:12:08,603
Didn't they say there were monkeys?

1973
01:12:08,914 --> 01:12:10,382
Shall we brush a monkey with that?

1974
01:12:11,002 --> 01:12:12,075
There's nowhere left for us to retreat to.

1975
01:12:12,076 --> 01:12:14,244
- What did you take out, Won Ji?
- My hat pouch.

1976
01:12:15,149 --> 01:12:16,413
We have nowhere to retreat.

1977
01:12:17,909 --> 01:12:20,551
If it's still over the weight limit,
that makes no sense.

1978
01:12:24,466 --> 01:12:25,313
This is...

1979
01:12:27,000 --> 01:12:28,926
(They put it on the scale.)

1980
01:12:29,180 --> 01:12:30,366
Hold on.

1981
01:12:30,393 --> 01:12:32,029
Seventeen, eighteen.

1982
01:12:32,121 --> 01:12:33,430
Take your hands off.

1983
01:12:37,241 --> 01:12:39,567
(How much will the suitcase weigh?)

1984
01:12:39,747 --> 01:12:41,887
- It's 19.65 kilograms.
- It's the same.

1985
01:12:41,888 --> 01:12:45,008
- This is crazy.
- It's the same.

1986
01:12:45,215 --> 01:12:46,577
It doesn't make sense.

1987
01:12:46,935 --> 01:12:49,855
(The same weight as last time.)

1988
01:12:50,022 --> 01:12:51,748
It's exactly the same down to the decimal.

1989
01:12:51,749 --> 01:12:53,917
I guess we really like 19.65.

1990
01:12:54,089 --> 01:12:55,686
Let's weigh it one more time.

1991
01:12:55,776 --> 01:12:57,120
I can't believe it.

1992
01:12:57,145 --> 01:12:57,988
(One more time.)

1993
01:13:01,249 --> 01:13:03,026
(It still weighs exactly 19.65 kilograms.)

1994
01:13:03,027 --> 01:13:04,661
- Still it's the same.
- Unbelievable.

1995
01:13:05,516 --> 01:13:06,930
This is unbelievable.

1996
01:13:06,948 --> 01:13:07,698
(In shock)

1997
01:13:07,699 --> 01:13:08,999
We didn't even add anything.

1998
01:13:09,132 --> 01:13:10,956
- At least it didn't get heavier.
- Exactly.

1999
01:13:11,363 --> 01:13:14,016
(All four strike
the exact same pose in shock.)

2000
01:13:14,036 --> 01:13:16,340
So we're at zero
in terms of the cost difference?

2001
01:13:16,423 --> 01:13:17,741
Nothing.

2002
01:13:18,136 --> 01:13:19,509
Maybe this is actually the best outcome.

2003
01:13:19,543 --> 01:13:22,008
Right. When you take out too much,
the next part gets difficult,

2004
01:13:22,009 --> 01:13:23,280
even though we get money.

2005
01:13:23,775 --> 01:13:26,416
We need to be more strategic now.

2006
01:13:27,484 --> 01:13:30,587
It might actually be better
to keep it at the same weight.

2007
01:13:31,021 --> 01:13:33,021
We're saving money for now,

2008
01:13:33,033 --> 01:13:35,359
and we can take things out
when we really need to.

2009
01:13:35,506 --> 01:13:36,560
When we're short on money.

2010
01:13:36,633 --> 01:13:38,562
- We're going into the jungle anyway.
- Right.

2011
01:13:38,593 --> 01:13:40,552
Let's not get too obsessed with it.

2012
01:13:40,553 --> 01:13:41,293
Okay.

2013
01:13:41,339 --> 01:13:42,900
Four of us at 19.65 kilograms total?

2014
01:13:42,939 --> 01:13:44,334
That's already unbelievable.

2015
01:13:44,366 --> 01:13:46,236
- It's impressive.
- It's 5 kilograms each.

2016
01:13:46,266 --> 01:13:47,638
Okay, let's pack up.

2017
01:13:47,639 --> 01:13:49,740
It's already seven.
We need to go to the airport.

2018
01:13:49,773 --> 01:13:50,874
It's past seven.

2019
01:13:51,119 --> 01:13:52,175
Let's just go.

2020
01:13:54,912 --> 01:13:58,198
(Time to leave for the next destination)

2021
01:13:58,265 --> 01:14:01,518
Even though the suitcase weighs the same,
we have more things to carry.

2022
01:14:02,026 --> 01:14:03,386
We have a lot in our hands.

2023
01:14:03,387 --> 01:14:05,022
(Arms full of stuff)

2024
01:14:05,023 --> 01:14:06,390
We're carrying lots of things.

2025
01:14:06,391 --> 01:14:08,091
(Is this really what emptying looks like?)

2026
01:14:08,439 --> 01:14:09,826
We should still bring our clothes.

2027
01:14:09,859 --> 01:14:12,028
- We need clothes.
- You really don't have many clothes.

2028
01:14:12,029 --> 01:14:15,832
(A suitcase, like memory,
is emptied only to be refilled.)

2029
01:14:15,833 --> 01:14:17,234
You have to buy something, Sian.

2030
01:14:18,249 --> 01:14:20,682
Buy something functional. Something long.

2031
01:14:20,683 --> 01:14:24,936
(What will happen
at the next destination?)

2032
01:14:26,089 --> 01:14:28,795
(What is the third destination?)

2033
01:14:28,902 --> 01:14:31,895
(The jungle village
of Bukit Lawang, Indonesia)

2034
01:14:32,062 --> 01:14:34,202
(A place where you can see orangutans)

2035
01:14:34,302 --> 01:14:37,775
(You will stay at the jungle village
without the suitcase.)

2036
01:14:37,968 --> 01:14:40,018
We'll buy what we need,
since we're going into the jungle.

2037
01:14:40,123 --> 01:14:42,446
(Already excited just preparing)

2038
01:14:42,706 --> 01:14:45,020
(Full gear and backpacks
instead of suitcases)

2039
01:14:45,293 --> 01:14:48,193
(Once everything is fully prepared,)

2040
01:14:50,046 --> 01:14:52,838
(They head into the jungle.)

2041
01:14:56,338 --> 01:14:59,277
(Cheerfully crossing
mountains and streams)

2042
01:14:59,478 --> 01:15:04,935
(Arriving at a luxurious accommodation
in the jungle)

2043
01:15:05,171 --> 01:15:10,250
(Even a lavish feast awaits them
before entering the jungle.)

2044
01:15:10,830 --> 01:15:11,455
(Sneakily)

2045
01:15:12,663 --> 01:15:13,722
(A guide suddenly appears.)

2046
01:15:13,723 --> 01:15:15,163
What kind of guide?

2047
01:15:15,482 --> 01:15:16,796
(We're going into the jungle now.)

2048
01:15:16,930 --> 01:15:18,236
(We'll be sleeping there.)

2049
01:15:18,790 --> 01:15:19,815
(Now?)

2050
01:15:22,094 --> 01:15:23,521
(There's just a tent.)

2051
01:15:23,694 --> 01:15:25,554
(An unexpected night sleeping outdoors)

2052
01:15:25,707 --> 01:15:27,761
(Today's roommates are
monitor lizards, monkeys, and insects.)

2053
01:15:28,387 --> 01:15:31,346
(No internet, Wi-Fi, or electricity)

2054
01:15:31,501 --> 01:15:34,025
(We're supposed to sleep here?)

2055
01:15:34,219 --> 01:15:35,945
(He suddenly shows them his scars.)

2056
01:15:36,132 --> 01:15:38,999
(There are king cobras too.)

2057
01:15:39,245 --> 01:15:41,285
(King cobras?)

2058
01:15:41,412 --> 01:15:42,512
(Jolts upright)

2059
01:15:42,872 --> 01:15:43,990
I'm leaving now.

2060
01:15:44,183 --> 01:15:46,396
I can't die here.

2061
01:15:46,397 --> 01:15:48,523
I still have so many things
I haven't done.

2062
01:15:48,877 --> 01:15:50,627
Are we going to be okay?

2063
01:15:51,370 --> 01:15:57,488
(The jungle survival story of four women)

2064
01:15:57,821 --> 01:16:01,447
(Even more shocking scenes await.)

2065
01:16:01,448 --> 01:16:03,808
(Disgusted)

2066
01:16:04,101 --> 01:16:06,462
(Will they be okay?)

2067
01:16:06,463 --> 01:16:07,704
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
